00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.470 align:start position:0%
 
technical leadership  what comes to your mind when you hear  these two words  as the name suggests the technical  leadership role consists of two main  responsibilities  technical responsibility and leadership  activity  in most organizations senior developers  who perform well are eventually asked to  lead a team and deliver results through  that team  they often become chief technology  officers and vice presidents of  engineering  some senior developers decide to take a  risk leave their organizations and  launch their own software startups  developers often assume new leadership  roles because of their deep technical  expertise that enabled them to perform  well in their technical roles  however after they become managers a lot  of them fail to become effective leaders  but why is that what many do not realize  is that leading requires an entirely new  set of traits  if you want to become a great tech lead  one day stay tuned as i explore the top  10 traits of the great technical leaders  first great technical leaders align  their teams with the company's vision  goals and strategy  each organization has an established  mission vision and strategy  vision defines long-term goals while  strategy formulates the ways of  achieving those objectives  great technical leaders know how to  communicate general companies vision  with their product design and technical  teams as well as align technical road  maps with the company's objectives in  order to maximize long-term shareholders  value  goals could include things like tripling  the user base increasing average revenue  per user by 40 percent doubling an  average user session or improving  loading times by 25 percent  based on specific objectives technical  leaders are able to define the direction  of the tech stack development what  features should be prioritized what  processes should be automated  what teams should be grown in-house  versus which should be outsourced and  what software components should be built  versus what should be bought  second great technical leaders know how  to establish trust and psychological  safety in their teams  google conducted a comprehensive  multi-year internal study to identify  the key factors that made their teams  more effective  psychological safety was far and away  the most important of the five dynamics  they found  so what happens when that all-important  psychological safety is absent in a tech  team  people become afraid to take risks and  innovate  they become more concerned with avoiding  mistakes than achieving big wins  developers tend to be naturally curious  independent creative and inventive  when you take away their autonomy they  feel cramped and unmotivated  when you let them relax and figure out  things on their own they blossom and  work magic  great technical leaders know that trust  and psychological safety is extremely  important in order to ensure a high  level of productivity of their technical  teams  three  great technical leaders know how to work  through failures and celebrate wins  technical leaders know that things will  fail deploys will fail schedules will be  missed  crashes will happen  however technical leaders do not worry  too much about failure  when things break great technical  leaders stay calm and don't look for  someone to blame  instead they take responsibility and use  their energy to fix the problem at hand  and learn from it  learning from failure shapes their  orientation and makes for better  decision making in the future  when an important feature is shipped or  a sprint is finished technical leaders  congratulate individual contributors as  well as organize fun activities with  their teams such as happy hours and teen  building activities  they know how to appreciate their team  members encourage them motivate them and  keep them happy  four  great technical leaders stay technical  one of the responsibilities of the  technical leaders is to oversee the  technical excellence of their products  to effectively accomplish this objective  great technical leaders stay technical  at all times  they are technically fearless and no  technical problem is impossible for them  they continuously work to expand both  the depth and breadth of their knowledge  in the problem domain technology and  best practices to keep up with the  growing demands of their work  technical leaders are either technically  the best of their teams or one of the  best  as such technical leaders define  technical vision for their products make  decisions on the technical stack  security and deployment practices as  well as are involved in code reviews and  technical mentoring of their staff  five technical leaders are biased for  action  knowledge and skills without action are  not sufficient to produce desired  outcome  therefore the top technical leaders  strive to be action oriented they  prioritize their tasks and act  immediately based on their priorities  actions are taken using practical tools  and processes  using a quick phone call rather than  writing a long email for example can be  more effective in acting for a priority  matter  sometimes bringing various stakeholders  in the same room with a clear agenda for  a short period of time can help resolve  a complicated matter quickly  excellent technical leaders are not only  action oriented by themselves but they  also enable others to become  action-oriented by facilitating the  activities making the approach easier  clearing the hurdles and providing a  clear vision  they value team consensus but in the  case of a prolonged technical discussion  without a decision technical leads drive  their teams to action  6.  technical leaders are quick learners  learning is a lifelong process  great technical leaders are quick  learners and they use every situation as  a learning opportunity  all quick learners have two  characteristics in common  first they are quick thinkers quick to  see problems and issues and quick to  imagine potential solutions  second they know how to collect  information from multiple sources turn  them into insight and bring practical  and real results using them  quick learners tend to pay more  attention to nuances think more  systemically and learn and apply  experiences to future possibilities  as a result they are more nimble and  effective in adapting recognizing and  anticipating problems early as well as  solving them responsively and  holistically  technical leads are balanced pragmatic  and realistic  they use their quick learning ability  judgment and experience to choose the  right trade-offs among competing  approaches  seven  great technical leaders are effective  communicators  they know that it is always better to  over communicate rather than under  communicate  effective communication is an inevitable  aspect of leading people dealing with  situations effectively and setting the  strategies for transformations  effective communication requires  unbiased listening understanding others  point of views and conveying the message  to the point in the right context  clarity is one of the critical enablers  of effective communication  using the right words in the right  context refraining from jargon and  ambiguous words are essential to  effective communication  excellent leaders articulate the  situations  however they do not just trust the power  of their communication but they also  find ways to validate the understanding  of other people  more importantly they follow up with  team members and other stakeholders  whether the message is understood and  appropriate actions are taken  eight great technical leaders are the  champions of understanding the why of  their work  they strive to understand where their  technical efforts fall into the  high-level business objectives  they also always keep their technical  teams aligned with the mission vision  and strategic goal nine great technical  leaders are self-aware  to be a self-aware leader you must know  who you are before you can look at  yourself in the context of your company  or in the context of your peers  you cannot be an effective leader  without emotional intelligence and  self-awareness  understanding yourself and your own  limitations what you are good at what  you are not good at is critical to  ensure you are surrounding yourself with  the right people  knowing this will allow you to better  focus on the people you interact with so  that you can recognize and interpret  what's happening within them and manage  your interactions with them based on  their emotions  a strong emotional intelligence  separates average from outstanding  technical leaders and is just as  important as iq  finally great technical leaders know how  to inspire lead and influence people  great technical leaders realize that the  key to success is deeply rooted in the  positive empowering leadership behaviors  that inspire people  you see a good leader can inspire people  to have confidence in the leader  a great leader can inspire people to  have confidence in themselves  today's technical experts are poised to  make strong influential leaders  to do so however they must rely on more  than their technical expertise  if you found this video useful i would  appreciate it if you smash the like  button  also make sure to subscribe to the  coding tech channel and click on the  notification bell  enjoy the rest of your day

